<title>USA: Sprint disappointed by federal court order.</title>
<headline>Sprint disappointed by federal court order.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sprint Corp said Tuesday it was disappointed by a U.S. court order that put on hold some of the landmark federal rules designed to open the nation's local telephone monopolies.</p>
<p>&quot;We're disappointed by the stay. We think it will delay the benefits of local phone competition for millions of Americans and will cause unnecessary confusion in the industry for months,&quot; a Sprint spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, a three-judge panel for the Eighth U.S. Circuit of Appeals suspended pricing rules that would have opened the local telephone markets to long-distance carriers, cable television operators and others.</p>
<p>--Kansas City bureau, 816 561-8671</p>
